BT /F1 8 Tf 0.40 0.47 0.52 rg 1 0 0 1 49 32 Tm (TECHNOLOGY / OPINION) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 0.40 0.47 0.52 rg 1 0 0 1 525 32 Tm (01) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 0.06 0.32 0.43 rg 1 0 0 1 49 739 Tm (THE ARGUMENT) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.4 Tf 0.22 0.43 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 49 709 Tm (A different kind of personal computer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 686 Tm (For decades, the personal computer has been organized around one assumption: the CPU is the center) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 670 Tm (of the system. Memory holds the data; the GPU assists with graphics and parallel workloads. Artificial) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 654 Tm (intelligence is forcing us to reconsider that arrangement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 626 Tm (The next PC may be defined less by how fast its CPU runs and more by the intelligence it can execute) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 610 Tm (locally: model size, available memory, memory bandwidth, usable context, response latency, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 594 Tm (ability of an AI agent to complete work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.8 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 560 Tm (The future of computing isn't a PC that runs AI. It's a PC that AI runs.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 0.06 0.32 0.43 rg 1 0 0 1 49 520 Tm (01 / The bottleneck in the traditional design) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 490 Tm (Consider a practical example. An NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti has approximately 448 GB/s of local) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 474 Tm (graphics-memory bandwidth. In an older system operating the card over PCIe 3.0 x8, the theoretical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 458 Tm (one-direction transfer rate between the GPU and the rest of the machine is only about 7.9 GB/s.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 430 Tm (Those numbers should not be confused with application speed: a GPU does not need to send every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 414 Tm (operation across PCIe. When model weights and the key-value cache remain in VRAM, most computation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 398 Tm (can proceed locally. The bottleneck becomes painful when a model or its working memory exceeds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 382 Tm (available VRAM and data must move repeatedly between GPU and system memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 354 Tm (The lesson is not simply that faster GPUs are needed. We also need more memory close to the compute) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 338 Tm (units, faster access to that memory, and software that avoids unnecessary transfers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.7 Tf 0.37 0.45 0.53 rg 1 0 0 1 220 32 Tm (By \301lvaro Augusto Pereira Lordelo Junior) Tj ET
endstream
