BT /F2 9 Tf 0.40 0.47 0.52 rg 1 0 0 1 525 32 Tm (02) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 0.06 0.32 0.43 rg 1 0 0 1 49 739 Tm (02 / What if we reverse the design?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 709 Tm (Imagine an architecture designed around a powerful GPU, with efficient CPU cores integrated to run) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 693 Tm (Windows or Linux, manage storage and networking, execute conventional applications, and coordinate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 677 Tm (AI agents. Both types of cores would share a large pool of high-bandwidth memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 649 Tm (Call this concept a CGPU: a GPU-centered computing platform with general-purpose CPU capabilities) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 633 Tm (built into the same tightly integrated system. The term here describes a design vision, not a specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 617 Tm (commercial product or a claim of invention.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 589 Tm (The goal would not be to eliminate CPUs. General-purpose operating systems still need strong) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 573 Tm (sequential performance, responsive interrupt handling, device management, and security boundaries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 557 Tm (Instead, it would make the AI engine a first-class part of the computer rather than an external) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 541 Tm (accelerator constrained by a separate pool of memory.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 0.06 0.32 0.43 rg 1 0 0 1 49 501 Tm (03 / AMD already has many of the ingredients) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 471 Tm (AMD has an unusual strategic position: it designs x86 processors, GPUs, interconnect technologies, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 455 Tm (platforms that bring the two together. Its Instinct MI300A combines Zen CPU cores and CDNA GPU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 439 Tm (compute with 128 GB of shared HBM3 memory, delivering up to 5.3 TB/s of theoretical memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 423 Tm (bandwidth. It is a high-performance computing product, not a consumer desktop, but it demonstrates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 407 Tm (the architectural direction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 379 Tm (Closer to personal computing, the Ryzen AI Max+ 395 combines Zen 5 CPU cores with integrated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 363 Tm (Radeon graphics and supports systems with up to 128 GB of memory and up to 256 GB/s of theoretical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 347 Tm (memory bandwidth. Meanwhile, NVIDIA's DGX Spark demonstrates a compact AI-focused system with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 331 Tm (128 GB of unified memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 303 Tm (The components of an AI-first architecture are not science fiction. The real challenge is turning them) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 287 Tm (into an accessible, reliable and developer-friendly PC.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 259 Tm (AMD also faces a software challenge: NVIDIA's CUDA ecosystem is deeply embedded in the AI stack.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 243 Tm (AMD's ROCm is improving, but hardware capabilities alone do not guarantee that models, drivers,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 227 Tm (libraries and agent frameworks will work seamlessly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.7 Tf 0.37 0.45 0.53 rg 1 0 0 1 220 32 Tm (By \301lvaro Augusto Pereira Lordelo Junior) Tj ET
