BT /F2 9 Tf 0.40 0.47 0.52 rg 1 0 0 1 525 32 Tm (03) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 0.06 0.32 0.43 rg 1 0 0 1 49 739 Tm (04 / An AI PC is not necessarily an AI-first PC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 709 Tm (Many machines are marketed as AI PCs because they include an NPU or accelerate a handful of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 693 Tm (intelligent features. That is useful, but it is not the full transformation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 665 Tm (In an AI-first PC, the operating experience itself changes. The user boots Windows or Linux, starts a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 649 Tm (local runtime such as Ollama, loads a model, and gives an agent access to approved tools. Instead of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 633 Tm (learning every application and performing every click, the user states an objective.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 605 Tm (The agent can then inspect information, open programs, draft documents, write code, coordinate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 589 Tm (workflows, or search an offline library. The human remains responsible for goals and authorization,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 573 Tm (particularly for irreversible operations, private data and system-level changes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 545 Tm (Traditional PC: the user operates applications to achieve a goal. AI-first PC: the user defines the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 529 Tm (goal; an agent operates applications under supervision. Core requirement: local capability, clear) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 513 Tm (permissions, auditable actions, and a way to stop or reverse mistakes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.8 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 485 Tm (The interface of the next PC may be less about where to click and more about what to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.8 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 469 Tm (accomplish.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 0.06 0.32 0.43 rg 1 0 0 1 49 429 Tm (05 / A new scoreboard for personal computing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 399 Tm (The specifications that matter will expand. CPU clock speed and core count will not disappear, but they) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 383 Tm (will be joined by metrics that describe how well a system actually runs useful AI workloads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 355 Tm (Model capacity: which models fit in memory without slow offloading? Memory performance: how much) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 339 Tm (bandwidth is available to the processor running inference? Responsiveness: what are the time to first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 323 Tm (token and sustained tokens per second?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 295 Tm (Working context: how much information can the model process accurately, not merely accept? Agent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 279 Tm (reliability: can it use tools, recover from errors and request approval when needed? Efficiency and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 263 Tm (privacy: can it work locally without sending sensitive information to remote servers?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 235 Tm (A large advertised context window does not guarantee strong reasoning. Nor does a high theoretical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 219 Tm (compute score guarantee good real-world inference. Memory architecture, optimized software and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 49 203 Tm (careful evaluation matter together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.7 Tf 0.37 0.45 0.53 rg 1 0 0 1 220 32 Tm (By \301lvaro Augusto Pereira Lordelo Junior) Tj ET
endstream
